Western ideas of what poetry is

228
00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:20.240
and how it works

229
00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:24.160
due to its extreme length constraints,
rejection of a lyrical subjectivity,

230
00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:27.200
and even a centering of meaning,
a type of literature that,

231
00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:30.480
even pre-digital, was seen as always,
inherently general.

232
00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:34.760
We can point us to other value systems
when it comes to the confluence

233
00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:36.640
of computation and writing.

234
00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:39.080
On the other hand,
an oversize, simplistic,

235
00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:42.560
oversimplified summary of such ideas
can itself fall into those

236
00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:45.840
orientalist traps
I discussed at the beginning of this paper

237
00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:49.840
into these maybe harmful ideas
about the general of Asia,

238
00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:52.840
always imitating
and never imitating and always imitating,

239
00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:55.920
but by juxtaposing these threads

240
00:13:55.920 --> 00:14:00.000
along with this enormously rich history
of generative poetics in Japan.

241
00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:04.080
I hope to show how much more interesting
and hard to sum up things actually are

242
00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:05.200
and have been.

243
00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:08.440
These aren't a final weapon, perhaps,
but to paraphrase

244
00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:12.600
who I quoted earlier,
they leave open a generative space

245
00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:15.640
where a strikingly vivid
wonder might still appear.

246
00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:16.640
Thank you so much.
